// Ch12 B04 side scene (optional): "The Knot" (E, 3 min, ~90 words). act2_ch12.md §4. An Ullari woman ties a
// knot on the pass-cord, touches it once and walks on without looking back. She isn't wise; she's tired and
// practical. No music. Then Rhen at the cord: he may tie a clumsy knot for his father, whom he believes dead;
// it is never named on screen.
title: ch12_the_knot
location: ch12/keth_pass
---
@camera P05
@music silence fade=1.0
@anim ullari_woman tie_knot
@wait 3.0
@mark ullari_woman road_down walk
@wait 1.5
@mark rhen road_down_catch walk
Rhen [neutral]: How do you do that? Just walk. #line:ch12_knot_001
@anim ullari_woman look_at rhen
@wait 2.0
Ullari_woman as "Ullari woman" [neutral]: My son. Last spring. On this road. #line:ch12_knot_002
Rhen [sad]: And you just walk on? #line:ch12_knot_003
Ullari_woman as "Ullari woman" [neutral]: I carry the knot. He doesn't have to. #line:ch12_knot_004
@mark ullari_woman road_away walk
<<set $ch12_heard_the_knot = true>>
@wait 2.0
@mark rhen knot_post walk
-> Tie a knot. #line:ch12_knot_005
    @anim rhen tie_knot
    @wait 3.0
    @mark rhen road_on walk
    <<set $ch12_rhen_tied_knot = true>>
-> Walk on. #line:ch12_knot_006
    @anim rhen look_at pass_cord
    @wait 3.0
    @mark rhen road_on walk
===
